		(uuid "08c03c41-829d-551f-97da-335e23d1fd15")
	)
	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page numbers at the bottom right of\nevery page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width. A dot joins lines; a cross on a pin\nend means the pin is not connected. Pins connect by net labels (the boxed names): pins whose labels\ncarry the same name are on one net, on any page. [3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too,\nits label in zone C4 (column 4, row C of the border). Click it to land on that label. No\n[page/zone]: the net is on this page only. Click a part's reference to find its row in the parts\nlist; the row's page/zone leads back. A part crossed out in red is not fitted (DNP). White: parts\nand their references. Grey: values, pin names, pin numbers. A dashed frame is a block of the\ncircuit, titled at its top left. An amber K5 marks a Kleidos addition or correction: it leads to\nits row below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bda0493-2ee9-55c7-a1cb-0a610274a847")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 87.135 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd5a92fc-7e34-5d85-88c6-51344be57ef1")
	)
	(text "Every part, pin and net of the StickC-Plus SE, with the values the vendor documents: connectivity\ndocumented from the vendor's public documentation, with Kleidos additions and corrections listed on\npage 1 (M5Stack's K016-P-SE schematic, one A4 sheet printed 2025-11-04, and its docs page, cited in\nREADME.md and netlist.yaml beside this file). Layout and symbols are this project's. No footprints,\nno PCB, no part numbers beyond the documented ones. Values are as the vendor prints them (5.1K,\n100uF/4V). A value of NC means not fitted: those parts (the IMU footprint U7, C21, C28, C29) are\nmarked DNP. Reference designators are the vendor's; the print leaves two parts without one: the\nESP32-PICO-D4 (\"U?\") is U1 here, the battery connector (\"Li_Ion\") is J3. Nets the print leaves\nunnamed carry names of ours (AXP_LX1, MOS1_G...). Wires that cross in the print without a junction\ndot are read as not connected: U1 pins 4 and 19 reach only C43 and C40, U6 pin 20 only C25\n(README.md, where pins 4 and 19 are open questions). U7's pin names are the MPU-6886 datasheet's\n(K28); U6's pin 10 is named P3.0, the datasheet's name (K1). Zones: columns 1-8 and rows A-F,\n50 mm apart, printed in the border."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 91.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0d9ecb2c-126e-52ac-a901-a174f0e3590c")
	)
